# DTF tier manifest: db-pool-fairness  (artifact-keeper#6344, 1.13.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + limits.db-pool (passes the pool sizing and
# admission knobs through to the backend).
#
# THE PROBLEM (#6344)
# The database admission gate of #4182 hands its slots to whoever arrives
# first, before authentication. An anonymous flood that holds every slot
# while the pool is busy gets every other client shed with
# 503 POOL_EXHAUSTED, authenticated users and CI tokens included.
#
# THE FIX (1.13.0)
# DATABASE_REQUEST_CREDENTIALED_RESERVE_PERCENT (default 25) of the slots can
# only be taken by a request presenting a credential (Authorization,
# X-API-Key, the session cookie, /t/<token>/), and a client at
# DATABASE_REQUEST_CLIENT_SHARE_PERCENT of the slots yields to a waiting one.
# This tier exercises the defaults; every request of the harness comes from
# one address, so it isolates the reserve.
#
# THE PRIMITIVE: A BUSY POOL WITH SPARE CONNECTIONS
# DATABASE_MAX_CONNECTIONS=12 and DATABASE_MIN_CONNECTIONS=12 (all open),
# DATABASE_REQUEST_CONCURRENCY=8 (on the fix 2 of them reserved by default),
# DATABASE_REQUEST_ACQUIRE_WAIT_MS=500. The oracle's own psql session takes
# ACCESS EXCLUSIVE on `repositories`, then sends 12 anonymous downloads of a
# public artifact one by one ("slow requests"); each one admitted blocks on
# the lock holding a pooled connection. The gate lets requests run without a
# slot while a quarter of the pool (3) is idle, so on both images the slow
# requests take connections until 2 are idle, and the rest are shed.
#   * main: the slow requests hold all 8 slots. An authenticated request finds
#     no slot and a busy pool, and is shed after the 500 ms wait, although 2
#     connections are idle.
#   * fix: anonymous requests may take 6 slots. The 2 reserved slots stay
#     free, and an authenticated request takes one and an idle connection.
#     Two spare connections leave room for one background query blocking on
#     the lock too.
# While the authenticated client polls, 6 anonymous loops keep flooding the
# same download.
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1):
#   (CONTROL) before the window: the anonymous download and GET
#             /api/v1/auth/me with the admin token answer 200. During the
#             window: the flood never gets a 2xx, and a wrong Basic password
#             is never 2xx. After the window: the slow requests complete,
#             and the download and /auth/me answer 200 again.
#   (FIX #6344) during the window at least 9 of 10 authenticated
#             /api/v1/auth/me requests answer 200. RED on main: 0 of 10,
#             each 503 POOL_EXHAUSTED.
#   (FIX #6344) the flood absorbs the sheds: ak_db_admission_sheds_total
#             counts anonymous sheds and no credentialed ones. RED on main:
#             no such series.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false so a 429 can never masquerade as either verdict.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem limits.db-pool"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
COVERS="6344"
export DATABASE_MAX_CONNECTIONS="12"
export DATABASE_MIN_CONNECTIONS="12"
export DATABASE_REQUEST_CONCURRENCY="8"
export DATABASE_REQUEST_ACQUIRE_WAIT_MS="500"
